-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance (Family Allowance) Regulations, 5720-1960 (תקנות הביטוח הלאומי (קיצבה משפחתית)). Row IL-33.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/national-insurance-family-allowance-regulations-5720-1960.he.wiki.txt
-- (Hebrew Wikisource raw wikitext, retrieved 2026-10-08T22:18:48Z, sha256 fcfeacc2...c80a3c).
--
-- WHAT IS LEFT OF THEM. The page's own note (line 14) says the Regulations were mostly cancelled and replaced
-- by the National Insurance (Claiming a Benefit and the Manner of Its Payment) Regulations, 5758-1998, which
-- are not deposited. Regulations 2 to 10 are each marked cancelled. What remains is: reg 1 (the period of
-- support for a child who is not the insured's own); reg 11 (a doubt about the continuation of the allowance);
-- reg 12 (commencement, 1 September 1959); reg 13 (the name). Reg 1 gives the period that s 65(a) "ילד"
-- paragraph (2) leaves to regulations (the note at line 807 of the Law names these Regulations); reg 11 limits
-- a suspension. Both are encoded. They refer to the Law by its 1953 numbering ("סעיף 104(א)(2)"), which is now
-- s 65(a) "ילד" (2): the Law's own note (line 807) says the Regulations under that paragraph are these.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Family Allowance Regulations — what remains of them`

§§ `Regulation 1 — the period of support`

-- src:19 | התקופה האמורה בפסקה (2) של הגדרת ”ילד“ בסעיף 104(א)(2) לחוק, היא שנים עשר החדשים הקודמים לתקופה שבעדה משתלמת הקיצבה המשפחתית בגלל אותו ילד.
-- "התקופה האמורה בפסקה (2) של הגדרת 'ילד' ... היא שנים עשר החדשים הקודמים לתקופה שבעדה משתלמת הקיצבה
-- המשפחתית בגלל אותו ילד": the twelve months before the period for which the allowance is paid for that child.
-- For a month, the period for which the allowance is paid is the month, and the twelve months before it end
-- on the day before the month's first day. A child who is not the insured's own counts under s 65 only if the
-- insured supported him in that period (row IL-06 takes "support proven" as an input; this is the period that
-- input is about).
@ref FA Regs reg 1, line 19; NII s 65(a) "ילד" (2), line 806
GIVEN `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`FA reg 1 — the first day of the period of support before the period beginning` `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid`) (DATE_MONTH `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid`) (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid` MINUS 1)

@ref FA Regs reg 1, line 19
GIVEN `the day`                                            IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`FA reg 1 — the day` `the day` `is in the period of support before the period beginning` `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST `FA reg 1 — the first day of the period of support before the period beginning` `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid`
    AND `the day` LESS THAN `the first day of the period for which the allowance is paid`

§§ `Regulation 11 — an allowance in doubt`

-- src:49 | הטיל המוסד ספק בקיום התנאים להמשך תשלום הקיצבה המשפחתית, כולה או מקצתה, רשאי הוא לדרוש מהאדם, שמשתלמת לו הקיצבה או שמכוחו משתלמת הקיצבה, פרטים וראיות בקשר לתשלום הקיצבה, ולהשהות תשלום הקיצבה עד לבירור הספק אך לא יותר מתשעים יום לאחר שהתעורר הספק. הודעה על ההשהיה ועל סיבותיה תימסר לתובע הקיצבה.
-- Regulation 11 (quoted above): The Institute may suspend payment until the doubt is cleared, but not more than 90 days
-- after the doubt arose. The 90 days are taken as ending ON the 90th day after the day the doubt arose
-- (fork F1, class (b)): "not more than 90 days after" is a limit, and the day 90 days after is within it.
@ref FA Regs reg 11, line 49
GIVEN `the day the doubt arose` IS A DATE
      `the day the doubt was cleared` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`FA reg 11 — payment may be suspended, a doubt having arisen on` `the day the doubt arose` `and been cleared on` `the day the doubt was cleared` `, on` `the day` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST `the day the doubt arose`
    AND `the day` AT MOST (`the day the doubt arose` PLUS 90)
    AND (CONSIDER `the day the doubt was cleared`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST cleared THEN `the day` LESS THAN cleared)
